# Tool input validation

| Field | Value |
| --- | --- |
| Issue | re-cinq/HALEngine#37 |
| Status | Draft |

The registered JSON Schema is the boundary between model-generated arguments and a tool executor.

## Contract

- The registry rejects missing required fields, wrong declared types and invalid enum members before executing a tool, returning a readable ToolResponse naming the property path and constraint without exposing input values in results or logs; valid arguments, including unknown keys, pass through exactly once without coercion or defaults, while an unknown tool name still throws.
- Static schemas are compiled at registration, invalid schemas throw an error naming the tool at registration, and ten executions reuse the compiled schema without rereading it.
- Function-valued definitions resolve for each execution and validate using the current schema, caching by resolved schema object rather than tool name.

## Delivery requirements

The implementation uses a JSON Schema validator in runtime dependencies, with no opt-out, and documents rejection as a tool result within the existing bounded tool loop in README.md, docs/adding-a-tool.md and .specify/spec.md.
The execute doc comment is one line pointing here; release notes and a MINOR version bump explain that executors no longer receive malformed arguments for custom error handling.
The existing orchestrator must carry a rejection back to the provider and permit a corrected retry within its five-round budget.
